WEBVTT

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.730
<b>The Stolen Rust Eater</b>

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.730
<b>The Stolen Rust Eater</b>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.360
Where the hell did you come from?!

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.620
Well, you sure are moving a lot 
better than before, aren't you?

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.750
Your life ends here, Man-Eating Akaboshi.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.620
Return my brother to me.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.300
First of all, Milo's the one who followed <i>me</i>.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:00.000
He wanted to save your life 
and that Rusted body of yours.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.040
Silver-tongued lies.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.770
You deceived my brother's pure heart with
 your baseless claims about this Rust Eater.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.070
Give him a little more credit!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.400
Haven't you ever heard
 of letting kids grow up?

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.770
Oh, right. You're his sister, aren't you?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:20.030
My bad. You look older, 
so I figured you were his mom.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.790
I'm going to crush you!

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.610
What is this?

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.290
Dumbass!

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.290
Toss the bike and get down!

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.310
Damn it.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.190
This is what happens when you 
start fights in dumb places.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.060
Bisco!

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.910
I'll get it to drop Pawoo!

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.580
Get ready to catch her!

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.430
Got it!

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.330
Milo!

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.350
If it flies any higher, 
you won't be able to get down!

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.460
Right!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.160
Milo!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.390
Get your bike up and running right now.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.770
<b>Imi</b>

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.770
Do it right now! You wanna 
watch your brother die?!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:42.440
<i>It's still not letting go, even after we 
dosed it with all that numbshroom?</i>

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:44.980
Actagawa.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.540
Do you believe in me?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.770
I'm sorry.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.480
All right!

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.020
<i>Bisco wouldn't give up!</i>

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.860
<i>Not until his very last arrow!</i>

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.870
I'm borrowing your staff!

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.360
Bisco!

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.320
Milo!

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.540
Milo!

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.380
Actagawa!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.120
I'm glad you're safe.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.020
Yeah.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:23.880
<b>Imi</b>

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.010
<b>Imi</b>

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:24.130
<b>Imi</b>

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.000
Why did you do something so reckless?

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:24.260
<b>Imi</b>

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.010
<b>Imi</b>

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.280
Isn't that obvious?

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.380
Because I absolutely 
don't want to lose you.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.130
Bisco, is this...

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.020
Yeah, it's the Rust Eater.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.590
We finally did it.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:51.020
Now we can cure Pawoo.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.680
Right, Bisco?

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.340
Bisco?

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.910
It's odd. Something's not right.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.290
Every mushroom has the 
power to consume Rust.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.760
It's only called the "Rust Eater" because 
it does it a lot better than other types.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.710
This thing's power to consume Rust, 
and even the way it tastes,

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.760
is no different from other matsutake.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.350
No way...

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.780
After all we went through for it?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.780
<b>Imi</b>

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.520
If we found the wrong one, 
that's all there is to it.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.780
We've got a little time before the sun sets.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.660
Let's hunt for our next prey.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.360
I understand how you feel, 
but we can't do that right away.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.950
It's clear you don't have blood to lose.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.270
Milo's right.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.950
None of us are really fit to fight right now.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.960
If you're worn out, I won't push you.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.080
I'll go by myself.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.120
Wait!

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:54.220
You're the most worn out of all of us!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:58.220
If you face one of those things in 
your condition, you'll die for sure!

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.670
Lose that overconfidence already!

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.970
I won't let it all be a waste 
after we've come this far!

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.710
Let go of me, dumbass!

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:06.370
Akaboshi!

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.000
Bisco!

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.070
Wait, the Rust Eater!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:25.750
I get it.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.620
It's Bisco's blood.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.050
All right.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.840
That's enough, right? What kind
 of trick did you pull earlier?

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.500
Your blood transfusion comes first.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.720
Bisco, what's your blood type?

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.930
What's a "blood type"?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.180
Blood is blood, isn't it?

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:48.760
Quit joking around. You must
 know your own blood type...

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.360
Blood type?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.570
What's that?

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:57.820
<i>Do Mushroom Keepers really 
have no concept of blood types?</i>

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.630
<i>Or it's more like their blood itself is...</i>

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.830
What's wrong? Can't you do
 it without knowing that?

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.630
No, it's fine.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:11.590
Jabi-san told me about the Rust Eater 
legends when we were in Imihama.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.570
What?!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.540
He never told me those!

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.100
I told you not to move.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.360
I thought it was strange.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:23.100
If the Pipe Snake was the seedbed for the
 Rust Eater, that didn't match the legends.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.530
You mean the Rust Eater 
growing on the Pipe Snake

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:29.620
only awakens after coming into 
contact with Mushroom Keeper blood?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:30.540
Yeah.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:34.340
Mushroom Keeper blood must 
have some mysterious factor to it.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:39.270
Bisco, once this artificial blood is done
taking, give me a bit of your blood.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:44.010
Why would Jabi keep quiet about that?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.700
Because if you took the 
legends at face value,

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:49.480
you might go sacrificing 
another Mushroom Keeper.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.800
I'd never do that to my friends—

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.770
Aren't you called the "Man-Eating Redcap,
 Akaboshi" precisely because you would?

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.630
Want me to bite you, bitch?

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:01.670
I told you not to move.
Are you incapable of staying still?

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:05.000
I can't just sit here wasting precious time!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.600
<i>The production of the Rust 
Eater is almost a riddle.</i>

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:18.780
<i>Such mysterious, yet effective, 
technique and pharmacology.</i>

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:23.280
<i>Perhaps Mushroom Keepers aren't the 
barbarians the world claims they are,</i>

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.260
<i>but rather, they are scientific saviors?</i>

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:32.200
<i>Though, if that is true, what about that tale?</i>

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.050
What are you lookin' at?

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.800
I'm going to go tune up my bike.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.760
It got pretty beat up, after all.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:01.950
I didn't count on you laying eyes 
on the legendary Rust Eater

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.790
while pursuing Akaboshi the man-eater.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.330
Kurokawa!

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:12.250
You could charm the government 
itself with such rare medicine.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:14.660
Imihama's governor, huh?

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.100
Nice to meet you, Akaboshi.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.940
Even after all that antibacterial 
treatment, it nearly bloomed.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.880
It won't be able to take multiple hits.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:39.670
Akaboshi, you're dangerous.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.660
I can't stop shaking.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.650
Hey, how long are you going to keep firing?

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:49.030
He's wounded! If we take him down here...

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:52.570
If you underestimate a 
Mushroom Keeper like that...

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:00.790
That's what's going to happen to you, dummy.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.350
Bisco!

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.820
<i>We'll meet again, won't we, Akaboshi?</i>

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.800
<i>That's our promise ring.</i>

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.830
That bastard used a Rust bullet.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.200
You sure you don't want
 to take an injection here?

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:35.310
I'll be fine.

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:38.340
If this cures old Jabi, I'll take one, too.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:39.740
But...

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.030
Right about now, Kurokawa will be sweating
 over the Rust Eater's lack of effect.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:51.720
If I show up fully healed, who knows what 
he'd resort to in order to figure out the trick?

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.230
You take care of Akaboshi.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:02.510
Either way, my bike's the only way to get this
 injection to old Jabi while he's still alive.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.540
I'll go to a Watch base for information
first. There's no need to worry.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:20.270
I'm no longer the one who
 can keep that boy safe.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.160
You are, Akaboshi.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.780
But this is your share.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.910
That stomach of yours.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:30.890
It might only look like a faint Rusting now,

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.640
but it'll probably progress
faster than a natural case.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.030
Use it if you need it.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.140
Pawoo, you...

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.490
You finally used my name.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:48.610
Just hurry up and defeat Kurokawa,
then you can come heal me.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.640
All right.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.120
Just a slight change to the order, then.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.490
If you're trying to make me owe 
you a favor, it doesn't count.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.770
Do you remember the first time we fought?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:12.070
You're the only one who's called me 
pretty after seeing my Rust, Akaboshi.

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:15.700
Now that I get a better look at you,
you're quite dashing yourself.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.400
You have a cute face.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:19.930
What?!

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.970
What are you two whispering about?

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:23.900
<b>Imi</b>

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.030
<b>Imi</b>

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:27.070
I was threatening him to 
make sure he protects you.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.780
<b>Imi</b>

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:36.210
<b>Imi</b>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.960
Shimobuki Tunnel

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.720
<b>Imihama Watch
Shimobuki Base</b>

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.610
Hey, what happened to the others?

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.710
Why isn't the Watch here?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.570
Those are some superhuman reactions.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:20.330
The fact that you can still move like that 
while wounded is absolutely terrifying.

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:21.960
Kurokawa.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.480
What did you do to my men?!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.710
Now, hold on a sec.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:31.980
Such a hot-blooded woman. Honestly...

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.400
We can talk after you've seen this.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:03.960
I'm back, Bisco.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.090
It's fried pig today...

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.920
Bisco!

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.730
Hey, Milo!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.850
Listen to this.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.480
This guy found a female swamp
 crab and ran off on his own.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.730
But without that big pincer he was
 so proud of, he got shot down.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:27.290
Guess you can't land a girl 
with a small pincer, huh?

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.240
I told you...

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.670
over and over not to move!

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.880
Why can't you listen when
 I tell you something?!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.770
Like I said, Actagawa ran off 
on his own and got rejected...

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:50.140
Oh, shit. I made him really mad.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.810
When he gets like that, he won't 
forgive me until I let him eat his fill.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.140
No, you idiot! Get back here!

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.230
I'll be ten minutes tops!

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.640
It's fried pig today, right?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:06.110
Skinning pigs is a pain, 
so I'll leave that to you!

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:10.770
That dumbass!

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:13.520
Here I am, worried sick about him,

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:17.060
and he doesn't show even a 
smidgen of cooperation. Honestly.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.650
<i>Uh, testing, testing. Testing, testing.</i>

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:27.080
<i>This is an official announcement from 
Imihama Prefecture's governor, Kurokawa.</i>

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.750
<i>This is a scheduled warning
 to wanted criminal</i>

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:35.110
<i>Akaboshi Bisco, as well as Nekoyanagi Milo.</i>

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:39.880
<i>You two must still be in 
Touhoku's broadcast range, right?</i>

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.970
<i>Then it's show-time.</i>

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:50.180
<i>I pray this video reaches you.</i>

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.010
Welcome back, Bisco.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.430
You made boiled pork?

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:18.570
Yeah, it had quite a lot of fat, so it would've
 been bad for your stomach otherwise.

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.090
I shaved off as much as I could
 and boiled the lean meat.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:25.440
Hey, c'mon, man. The fat's the best part of a pig...

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.040
Hm? What's the matter?

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.360
Sleepshroom poison.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.600
What's going on? Why the hell 
would you try and pull this?

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:46.620
Bisco, please...

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.630
Listen to me—

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.630
It's Pawoo, isn't it?

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:53.270
The Shimobuki base, right? I know where it is.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:05.280
Bisco!

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.240
You can't! Hold on!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.610
This is your sister here!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.190
Is now really the time to be scared?!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:17.870
I'm telling <i>you</i> not to go!

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:20.460
I'm a doctor.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:23.890
Did you think I wouldn't notice
you've been suffering?

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:28.240
I know your organs are a wreck 
from the wounds and poison.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:32.030
You can cover up your Rusted side, 
but I can tell you can't deliver a real kick.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.580
I can tell your vision's blurry 
and you're shooting on instinct.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:36.790
I knew all of it.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:42.000
You're far sicker than Pawoo or even Jabi-san!

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:46.820
There's no way you'll make it back if 
you go risking your life in your state!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.670
So what?

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.840
Whatever happens, it's my life.

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:54.220
Why would I have any obligation to 
let you take care of me like that?

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.500
Because we're friends, aren't we?!

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:59.990
Isn't your obligation there obvious?

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:03.490
There's no way you and I don't owe each other!

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:07.990
You are my most treasured friend,

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.870
and I don't want you to die.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:13.200
Isn't that obvious?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.210
Why wouldn't it be obvious?!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.130
I'd say the same thing right back, Milo.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:29.110
People need you a lot more than they need me.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.900
If either of us should die first, it's me.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.270
You just stay right here.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.040
I'll be right back.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.770
I'm not letting you go.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.360
Even if I have to risk everything.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:48.500
You know what I'm truly capable 
of better than anyone else, Milo.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:53.740
And you know what I do to people
who draw a bow on me, too.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:20:02.540
Yes, I know. But you never taught me 
to lose to a sick man at death's door.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.720
You're still years behind me!

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.480
If you get it now, then settle d—

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:23.530
You're the one who should settle down, Bisco!

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.740
Bring it on, then!

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.500
I won't let you go!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.970
Never!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.310
Oh, shit.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.210
Milo!

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.660
I'm sorry, Bisco.

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.120
Dummy, don't apologize.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.360
I made up my mind.

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:14.540
This time, I'll shield you from as many 
wounds as you've taken on my behalf.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.170
I'll be your spear, as well.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:23.170
I'll risk this slight body of mine along 
with my heart and soul to make sure...

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.460
to make sure I protect you.

